I am reaching out to talk about a newer program the Red Cross is now offering elementary schools.&nbsp; This program teaches students about the Red Cross, and the important role they play in both disaster and blood collection.&nbsp; This program is age appropriate learning and the schools that have participated have had great success for the student&rsquo;s involvement, family/PTA participation, and of course the many patients and local hospitals in need.&nbsp; I have included a very brief summary of the program and would welcome a conversation sometime in the next few weeks with a thought on launching the program in the beginning of 2018, and example timeline would be to talk with the students Jan-Feb, and run the drive 3-4 weeks after that.&nbsp; I look forward to your thoughts on this.<br />
